    "updated_at": "2026-11-21T09:18:01Z",
    "body": "Second red, same test: run 44887183876 on main fa00f79db fails wide_rectangular_pocket_is_cleared_by_parallel_lanes in 140 s (flagged slow, over 60 s). The diff from the first red tip is only PR #3054, which changes crates/sim verify code and its tests - no crates/motion file. The motion tree has been unchanged since the green tip 11402dba4.\n\nPattern so far: green at 64 s (11402dba4), red at 145 s (8be100737), red at 140 s (fa00f79db); a targeted local batch run on 8be100737 passed without a change. That fits a wall-time-sensitive test that fails only when the runner shares its cores with other builds. It is not a code regression in the merged window.\n\nFix path (held by @mkinney, branch issue/3116-parallel-lane-timing): remove the runner-load assumption from the test - no wall-time bound in an assertion; move it out of the default suite or give it a larger fixture per AGENTS.md, \"A test that takes more than about 60 s in debug moves to the heavy lane\".\n",
    "author_association": "OWNER",
    "pin": null,
